%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8457553d7570b1146a94bd661e6d7528, type: 3}
  m_Name: Grand Coalition Mission
  missionName: Grand Coalition
  description: "No single faction can govern effectively while the constitutional order remains deadlocked. Resolve 2 genuine faction demands and assemble enough political cooperation to make government possible again."
  flavorText: "{FactionDemandSummary} Neither side is likely to receive everything it wants, and that may be the foundation on which a settlement can actually stand. Rivals who disagree on policy, leadership, and perhaps even the meaning of the constitution must now decide whether preserving the state matters more than defeating one another today. Offices may be shared, reforms exchanged, and compromises written carefully enough that each faction can claim it protected something essential. A coalition formed under pressure may be inelegant. Government does not always require elegance; sometimes it requires enough people to stop saying no at the same time."
  splashImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 2f5257944414f8247a0d92243b7089b7, type: 3}
  victorySplashImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: a416f85ab061dfd40bb9c721e8f927cc, type: 3}
  failureSplashImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 645c8124084c884438b0347b884cab0c, type: 3}
  victoryFlavorText: "The coalition agreement is complete, and rival blocs now share enough responsibility to keep the state functioning. Faction leaders still quarrel, but they are quarrels inside government rather than against it. Policy moves again through institutions instead of blockades and boycotts. The constitution survives because enough opponents chose coexistence over collapse."
  failureFlavorText: "Coalition talks failed before sufficient demands were resolved. Every faction blamed another for bad faith, and each collapsed negotiation made maximalism look safer than compromise. Administrative routine decayed while leaders argued over legitimacy itself. The crisis deepens because no one could assemble a governing majority willing to own the burden together."
  participantRole: 0
  strategyTags: 88
  objectives:
  - objectiveName: Grand Coalition
    description: "Resolve 2 faction demands during the constitutional crisis."
    type: 37
    targetValue: 2
    targetMode: 0
    targetMultiplier: 1
    minimumTarget: 0
    maximumTarget: 0
  constraints: []
  rewardTiers:
  - tierName: Complete
    requiredObjectivesCompleted: 1
    rewardLegacy: {fileID: 11400000, guid: c089dcfb914340489c981c0521933ea0, type: 2}
